From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:18:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] feat(qti): extend reboot-reason cookie stash to
 lemans/kodiak/monaco

qti_pmic_prepare_reset2() only stashes the SYSTEM_RESET2 reboot-reason
cookie (PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE / TCSR_BOOT_MISC_DETECT) on platforms that
define both registers, which so far was shikra alone.

Downstream TZ's psci_target_system_reset2() ASIC hooks for lemans,
kodiak and monaco use the same cookie-stash scheme as shikra, but with
a different PMIC PON scratch register: reset_info_config.addr is
0x7148 for all three (vs. shikra's 0x88F), consistent with their PON
block using different offsets for PON_PS_HOLD_RESET_CTL/CTL2 (0x852/
0x853 vs. shikra's 0x85A/0x85B). TCSR_BOOT_MISC_DETECT is their shared
QTI_CORE_TOP_CSR_BASE (0x01f00000) plus the fixed 0xC0000 + 0x13000
offset, giving 0x1FD3000 - already present and used at that same value
in lemans's and kodiak's qti_secure_io_cfg.h.

Define both registers for lemans_def.h, kodiak_def.h (covers rb3gen2
and sc7280_chrome) and monaco_def.h (covers monza), so these platforms
get the cookie-stash behavior instead of compiling it out.

qcs615 and sc7180 are left out: downstream TZ has no ASIC
implementation for either, and neither defines QTI_CORE_TOP_CSR_BASE,
so there's no way to derive TCSR_BOOT_MISC_DETECT, nor a reference
reset_info_config.addr for PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/pull/134]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 plat/qti/hoya/kodiak/inc/kodiak_def.h | 5 +++++
 plat/qti/hoya/lemans/inc/lemans_def.h | 5 +++++
 plat/qti/hoya/monaco/inc/monaco_def.h | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/qti/hoya/kodiak/inc/kodiak_def.h b/plat/qti/hoya/kodiak/inc/kodiak_def.h
index 9d02329ca..af09dd433 100644
